From fc4a8dce713fcd329bf67ae3fb5994c49d0a83b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:36:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] verify/aeneas/forge-bool-core: the translation moves into
 verify/aeneas, built by the canonical tools

- research/kernel-audit/decide-once/aeneas/{lean,README.md} move to verify/aeneas/forge-bool-core;
  translate.conf (whole crate, release with overflow checks, BRIDGE=none: no f64) replaces
  the research translate.sh.
- Types/Funs regenerated by tools/aeneas/translate.sh: the same definitions (670) as before,
  without the module header.
- FunsExternal.lean: no axioms. Bool::ne, the tuple eq/ne (std's bodies) and Vec::default
  are defs; the Hash impls and the tuple Debug are Lean opaques.
- lakefile/manifest: forge-exact by its new relative path; Aeneas at the pinned commit.
- tools/aeneas, .github/workflows/aeneas.yml (translation-fresh and lean jobs) and the
  Cargo exclude for verify/aeneas, from claude/repo-review-mbdrlj-aeneas.

translate.sh forge-bool-core --check is clean; lake build passes (3750 jobs),
Axioms.lean included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
